  "answer": "Found the bug: `total()` subtracts each amount. Let me check the test and runner before fixing.\nThe test expects `[4, 6] → 10`, `[] → 0`, `[-3] → -3` — pure addition. Fixing the single offending line:\nFixed and verified — test passes.\n\n**The bug:** In `src/ledger.ts`, the `total()` accumulator used `sum -= entry.amount`, so every entry was subtracted. `total([{ amount: 4 }, { amount: 6 }])` returned `-10` instead of `10`, and a negative entry like `{ amount: -3 }` wrongly became `+3`.\n\n**The fix:** Changed that one line to `sum += entry.amount`, so entries accumulate additively.\n\n**What was preserved:**\n- Exported shape unchanged: `interface Entry { amount: number }` and `export function total(entries: Entry[]): number` are intact.\n- `test/oracle.test.ts` untouched, no new config or runner changes (per AGENTS.md).\n\n**Test result:** `bun test` → 1 pass, 0 fail (3 assertions): `[4, 6] → 10`, `[] → 0`, `[-3] → -3`."
